  "conventions": "the rows have the shape of the negative_certificates rows of finality_v1.json, with `transcript` in place of `dst`: byte strings are 0x-prefixed lowercase hex, and `expected.evm`/`expected.ton` name the \u00a75.2.2 outcome of VerifyCertificate steps 1\u201312 on a fresh destination deployed with `pin` at `now_ms`. `now_ms` is the destination clock: block.timestamp (EVM) or now() (TON) in whole seconds, times 1000, so every `now_ms` is a multiple of 1000. The test keys, the committee and the verification context are those of finality_v1.json; a row is well formed up to the pairing check, the only step a foreign transcript can fail",
